// live in. Payload's own docs say so ("existing data for this field will be
// lost"). The edits:
//
// 1. Every value is copied into its `_locales` table as `en` *before* any
//    column is dropped — main tables and `_posts_v`, so version history keeps
//    its text too. One `en` row per parent, values or not, which is what
//    Payload writes on every save.
// 2. `modified_at` (en) is seeded from `updated_at`, row for row, so the
//    English sitemap lastmod, JSON-LD `dateModified` and `og:modified_time`
//    read exactly the values they read before. See `stampLocaleDates`.
// 3. The nav arrays' new `_locale` column is added nullable, filled with `en`,
//    then made NOT NULL — the generated `ADD COLUMN … NOT NULL` fails on a
//    table that has rows.
// 4. `down` copies `en` back into the old columns, and refuses while any
//    translation exists unless DOWN_DISCARDS_TRANSLATIONS=1, because the old
//    shape has nowhere to keep one.
//
// `pnpm i18n:migration-counts` prints the row and value counts this must
// preserve, before and after. docs/LOCALIZATION.md has the production steps.

